## Building a Validation Module

### The Validator Interface

```xiom
interface Validator {
  fn validate(&self, input: Str) -> Bool;
  fn error_message(&self) -> Str;
}
```

Every validator answers: 'is this valid?' and 'what should I say if it fails?'

### Email Validator

```xiom
type EmailValidator {}

fn EmailValidator.validate(&self, input: Str) -> Bool {
  input.contains("@") && input.contains(".")
}

fn EmailValidator.error_message(&self) -> Str {
  "Must be a valid email address"
}
```

### Age Validator

```xiom
type AgeValidator { min_age: Int; }

fn AgeValidator.validate(&self, input: Str) -> Bool {
  let n = input.len();
  n > 0 && n <= 3
}

fn AgeValidator.error_message(&self) -> Str {
  "Must be a valid age"
}
```

### Using the Module

```xiom
mod validators {
  pub use email_validator::EmailValidator;
  pub fn validate_all[T: Validator](v: &T, input: Str) {
    if !v.validate(input) {
      io.println(v.error_message());
    } else {
      io.println("Valid!");
    };
  }
}
```

